    597  4bea					      subroutine
    598  4bea							; following the keytar: the beat runs on by itself, and each of its beat
    599  4bea							; clocks corrects it. k = steps of this beat already played:
    600  4bea							;   0		the clock is ahead of us: this beat starts now
    601  4bea							;   1 .. spb/2  we're in step: the rest of the beat counts from the clock
    602  4bea							;   more	 the clock is early: skip to the next beat, starting now
    603  4bea							; (After a keytar Start, step 1 waits for the first clock: beatWait.)
